Description: Kidux daemon: children, their time, and who may change them
 Kidux is a Debian derivative for a child's first computer. This package is
 the one part of it that runs with privileges: it keeps the family's settings,
 creates and removes the children's accounts, checks the adult password, and
 is the only thing that decides what a child may do.
 .
 Everything a child's session runs can eventually be stopped or changed by
 the child, so nothing a child runs is trusted with any of that. The sign-in
 screen, the lock screen and the adult panel all ask this daemon, and are
 told yes or no.
